# The update notice (crates/chipload-gui/src/app/update_notice.rs, docs/specs/update-notice.md).

updates-ask = Check for new versions of Chipload? Once a day the app asks GitHub for the latest release; nothing about you or your projects is sent.
updates-ask-yes = Check
updates-ask-no = Don't check
updates-ask-close-hover = Ask again next time
updates-available = Chipload { $version } is available
updates-available-hover = A newer version is on GitHub
updates-whats-new = What's new…
updates-whats-new-hover = The release's page on GitHub, in your browser
updates-skip = Skip this version
updates-skip-hover = No notice for { $version }; a later version shows
updates-check-now = Check for new versions now
updates-checking = Checking for new versions…
updates-latest = Chipload { $version } is the latest version
updates-failed = Could not reach GitHub: { $reason }
updates-setting = New versions
updates-setting-check = Check once a day
updates-setting-hover = Asks GitHub for the latest release once a day; nothing about you or your projects is sent. Help > Check for new versions now works either way.
